From: challoc <noreply@chainguard.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] zmalloc: free large objects and keyspaces through
 challoc_free_batch (proof of concept)

Valkey 9.1.2 (tag 9.1.2, commit 7f1dffedff6de73058b2c2a389422b6ecd56c8fb),
on top of 0001 (MALLOC=challoc) and 0002 (the usable-size entry points).

Tearing down a large set, hash, sorted set or list, or a whole keyspace
(FLUSHALL, FLUSHDB, and their lazyfree jobs on the bio thread), frees its
elements in bucket order, which is no address order: challoc's thread
cache then flushes half a cache at a time spread over thousands of slabs,
and the flush's address sort and one-or-two-slots-per-slab releases were
about a third of the teardown's time.

zfree_defer_begin() and zfree_defer_end() bracket freeListObject,
freeSetObject, freeZsetObject, freeHashObject, kvstoreEmpty and
kvstoreRelease. In between, this thread's zfree and zfree_with_size
collect their pointers (ZFREE_DEFER_N, 4096 by default) and release them
with challoc_free_batch (<challoc/challoc.h>), which runs free's checks on
every pointer, sorts the batch and releases each slab's slots together;
its return, the usable bytes freed, goes to used_memory. Nothing freed in
a bracket is reused before the bracket's flush.

challoc_free_batch is a weak reference: on a libchalloc.so.0 without it
nothing is deferred and the server runs as without this patch.
---
diff --git a/src/kvstore.c b/src/kvstore.c
index 71d1068..decf5e8 100644
--- a/src/kvstore.c
+++ b/src/kvstore.c
@@ -313,6 +313,7 @@ kvstore *kvstoreCreate(hashtableType *type, int num_hashtables_bits, int flags)
 }
 
 void kvstoreEmpty(kvstore *kvs, void(callback)(hashtable *)) {
+    zfree_defer_begin();
     for (int didx = 0; didx < kvs->num_hashtables; didx++) {
         hashtable *ht = kvstoreGetHashtable(kvs, didx);
         if (!ht) continue;
@@ -333,9 +334,11 @@ void kvstoreEmpty(kvstore *kvs, void(callback)(hashtable *)) {
     kvs->bucket_count = 0;
     if (kvs->hashtable_size_index) memset(kvs->hashtable_size_index, 0, sizeof(unsigned long long) * (kvs->num_hashtables + 1));
     kvs->overhead_hashtable_rehashing = 0;
+    zfree_defer_end();
 }
 
 void kvstoreRelease(kvstore *kvs) {
+    zfree_defer_begin();
     for (int didx = 0; didx < kvs->num_hashtables; didx++) {
         hashtable *ht = kvstoreGetHashtable(kvs, didx);
         if (!ht) continue;
@@ -351,6 +354,7 @@ void kvstoreRelease(kvstore *kvs) {
     if (kvs->hashtable_size_index) zfree(kvs->hashtable_size_index);
 
     zfree(kvs);
+    zfree_defer_end();
 }
 
 unsigned long long int kvstoreSize(kvstore *kvs) {
